{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["And you shall treat them as uncircumcised — the sense is blocking, sealing, and removal. ערלה אזנם. ערל לב. שתה גם אתה והערל."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The lemma and explanation refer to Leviticus 19:23 (וערלתם ערלה); the three closing examples are unvocalized biblical phrases illustrating the root ערל as metaphorical blockage: 'their ear is uncircumcised' (Jeremiah 6:10), 'uncircumcised of heart' (Leviticus 26:41 / Ezekiel 44:7,9), and 'drink, you too, and become uncircumcised' (Jeremiah 25:27, where the qere reads והערל)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:05.600783677Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}